# 0087-deleted-game-leaves-shader-preparation-cover-kept-no-blue.patch -- the owner's point Q after 0086: a deleted game's cloud card that said "Preparing the shaders" for ever, had lost
# its cover, and was drawn in blue. Applies after 0086. UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR: compiled, and its pure part ran in the host harness (below).
#
# Q. After the owner deleted South Park (its build and its file), its card was back in the cloud ("On the NAS", Download) but still said "Preparing the shaders · South Park … · 5,009 of 5,…"
#    with a full bar, for ever. Cause (GameAppWarm.cs GameWarm): Stop bumped the run's number but left the run ACTIVE; only the end of the CURRENT run cleared it, and a stopped run is never
#    current again. So EVERY stop (a delete, Play, an export, the owner's Pause) left a frozen "active" run with its last counts: on the card of its title (whatever its state: the strip only
#    compared the title id), in the menu's Pause, the sheet's "Preparing", the Build tab, and the queue never started again (WarmKick waits for no active run) until iBuilder was quit; "Delete
#    the build" was refused meanwhile (its Busy included the preparation). NOW:
#    - Stop ends the run at once (WarmRun, GameAppField.cs: a number and an on/off; a late thread of an older run never ends a newer one); the next run's thread waits for the stopped one's
#      to be gone (its workers finish the library they are on), so one run's workers at a time write warmed.tsv.
#    - The preparation's line, bar and Pause show on a BUILT game only (WarmShown.On: the card, the sheet, so the iPad inspector, the menu), whose run is going or which is the paused queue's
#      first: never on a cloud card, a download, or a game whose build or file was deleted.
#    - "Delete…" stops the run (StopWarm: its continued-processing task and lock-screen / Dynamic Island progress end), takes the title out of the queue BEFORE the files go (log
#      "shader warm-up: <game> left the queue (deleted)"), and removes its markers (games/<id>/warmed.tsv, prepared.tsv; games/<id>/ whole with the saves): a later build is prepared again.
#      Deleting only the build (after a full export) does the same: the run when it is that title's, the queue entry, the markers, then the next game goes on (WarmSync); the preparation
#      no longer blocks that delete.
#    - Its cover stays when the cloud still lists the title (CoverKeep.OnDelete: a base game of that title id in the listing, any name or case): games/<id>/icon.jpg and the person's own
#      cover are not deleted (keeping the saves), or are put back after games/<id>/ went (with the saves); the question says "Its cover stays: the game is still in the cloud." The cloud
#      card draws it greyed, as any cloud cover; the NAS cover pass (0084) is not needed for it.
#    - "On the NAS" (and the cloud dot) in the muted ink, the design's ink at 60 % (it was #A9BDF5, a light blue); the storage bar's segments lose their blue and violet too (accent, green,
#      ink at 60 % and 34 %, then the free space).
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-22, M1 Pro): check-patches-apply.sh: every patch applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree. Compile (-t:Compile):
#   0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code as before 0080. Host harness (harness87: … P86;P87): 270 of 270 checks (22 new: the run's on/off, delete during and after the
#   preparation and with the queue paused -> no line, the title out of the queue; the deletion plans with and without the cloud; the wiring); 12 of 12 mutations killed.
# NOT VERIFIED: nothing ran on a device: the end of the lock-screen progress at a delete, the kept cover on the real cloud card, the new colours' look.
# NEW UI STRINGS: "Its cover stays: the game is still in the cloud."; log lines "shader warm-up: … left the queue (deleted)", "shader warm-up: … left the queue (its build is deleted)",
#   "delete: the cover of … is kept: the game is still in the cloud".
